THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This software incorporates third-party open-source components, each licensed by
its respective copyright holders. The majority are distributed under permissive
licences (MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, PSF). Two categories carry
obligations that survive into a proprietary distribution and are recorded here
explicitly rather than left for a reader to discover:

  LGPL-3.0-only
    psycopg, psycopg-binary — the PostgreSQL database adapter.

    Used as an unmodified, separately installed library, imported at runtime. It
    is neither modified nor statically linked, and nothing in this software
    prevents a recipient from replacing it with another copy or version of the
    same library. Where this software is distributed (as opposed to operated as a
    hosted service), the full text of the GNU Lesser General Public License
    version 3 is provided with the distribution, and this notice satisfies the
    attribution requirement.

  MPL-2.0
    certifi, pathspec — DEVELOPMENT TOOLING ONLY.

    Measured, not assumed: an SBOM of an environment built to mirror the shipped
    Dockerfiles contains 35 components and neither of these is among them. They
    are declared here because they appear in development environments and because
    the CI copyleft gate treats them as known; they are not distributed with this
    software. MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft and neither is modified.

A machine-readable inventory of every dependency and its licence is published as
a CycloneDX SBOM alongside each release.

Nothing in this section grants any additional rights in the proprietary portions
